|name2 = Iz the Lady of Mourning
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Iz the Lady of Mourning''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit has a bit of everything, which makes her quite easy to use. While she may struggle against ranged, powerful enemies like [[Professor A.]] or [[Le'noir]], or Metal Enemies, she can work well against pretty much everything else. The low cost and good stats make her a decent pick even against common traited enemies, resulting in one of the safest picks when challenging stages without knowing their content. The biggest thing to look out for is her range. Iz the Lady of Mourning has a tendency to get way closer to the enemy frontline than you may want her to, only to start her somewhat slow-ish attack animation, which can easily be interrupted. The fast speed and immunity to everything do not help. For this reason, she is best paired with de-buffers, fast meatshields and anything that could get around enemy waves or surges.

While she may be brought into a fight for one or more abilities in particular, there are some that don't exactly stand up on their own. Namely, while her Zombie Killer is helpful, her stats are not great for killing zombies, meaning that she shouldn't be picked above specialized anti-Zombie units. A similar thing is true for most [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] enemies, as she will get destroyed by the likes of [[Super Hyppoh]] since she can't tank them. However, she does pretty well against [[Big Peng Z]] due to most of his damage being in his [[Toxic]], which she's immune to.

She also works very well as a [[Shield Piercing|Shield Piercer]] and decently as a [[Barrier Breaker]], serving as one of the few units with these abilities that has forward piercing [[Omni Strike]] with no considerable downsides. This makes her an excellent option at handling low level peon spam, such as [[Miz Devil]]s, [[Aku Doge]]s, and [[UltraBaaBaa]]s. She has enough HP to get to the frontline and pierce shields most of the time, and her 100% proc along with cheap cost and short recharge time means she is one of the best and most consistent shield piercers in the game. Not only that, her status as a rusher type unit can make her phenomenal at dealing with slower attacking threats such as [[Wicked Face]], [[Ackey]], [[Ribbo]], and other enemies that rely on gimmicky status effects to breach your defenses; since she's immune to practically everything, she can be used for practically everything as long as you time her correctly.

Keep in mind, against enemies like [[Le'Behemoth]], [[Youcan]], or [[Fallen Bear]], she oftentimes dies too quickly to be of much use. Her damage is pitiful against traited enemies, which means her utility ends at the Shields and Barriers which she rids enemies of. Measure her cost to her effectiveness so that you don't drain your cash and potentially lose due to poor timing or bad financial decisions. This isn't real life, after all.

